## 📋 PHASE 2 — Architecture

### 2.1 System Architecture
- [ ] Architecture diagram (C4 Level 1 — System Context)
- [ ] Architecture diagram (C4 Level 2 — Container)
- [ ] Architecture diagram (C4 Level 3 — Component, for complex services)
- [ ] All system components listed (Frontend, Backend, DB, Cache, Queue, CDN, etc.)
- [ ] Communication patterns between components (sync REST, async messaging, gRPC, WebSocket, GraphQL)
- [ ] Network topology (VPC, subnets, load balancers, reverse proxy)
- [ ] Data flow diagrams (user request → frontend → API → service → DB → response)
- [ ] Authentication/authorization flow diagram
- [ ] All external integrations listed with owners and contracts
- [ ] All third-party APIs with rate limits, SLAs, and fallback strategies
- [ ] All internal microservices this system interacts with
- [ ] Message broker topology (Kafka topics, RabbitMQ exchanges, SQS queues)
- [ ] File storage architecture (S3, Azure Blob, local filesystem)
- [ ] CDN configuration (CloudFront, Akamai, etc.)
