## 📋 PHASE 6 — Deployment

### 6.1 Release Process
- [ ] Release cycle frequency (weekly, bi-weekly, sprint-based, continuous, on-demand)
- [ ] Who owns / coordinates the release (Dev Lead, Release Manager, DevOps)
- [ ] Release approval process (change advisory board, PO sign-off, QA sign-off)
- [ ] Release versioning scheme (SemVer, date-based, build number)
- [ ] What artifacts are released (Docker image tags, JAR versions, frontend bundles)
- [ ] Release notes / changelog process (auto-generated, manual, tool)
- [ ] Release branch strategy (release branch cut, feature freeze, code freeze)
- [ ] Release calendar (scheduled dates, blackout periods)

### 6.2 Frontend Deployment — Step by Step
- [ ] Build command for production (`ng build --configuration=production`)
- [ ] Build output location (`dist/` folder structure)
- [ ] Where the built artifact is deployed (S3 + CloudFront, Nginx, Azure Static Web Apps, Netlify, container)
- [ ] How deployment is triggered (CI/CD pipeline, manual script, CLI command)
- [ ] CDN cache invalidation process after deploy
- [ ] How environment-specific config is injected at build time vs. runtime
- [ ] How to verify the correct version is deployed (version file, build hash in footer)
- [ ] Source maps — are they deployed? Where? Access-restricted?

### 6.3 Backend Deployment — Step by Step
- [ ] How the backend is packaged (Docker image, fat JAR, WAR, native executable)
- [ ] Docker image build process (Dockerfile reviewed, multi-stage, base image)
- [ ] Container registry push process
- [ ] Deployment method (K8s `kubectl apply`, Helm upgrade, ECS task update, systemctl, Ansible)
- [ ] Database migration step — before or after app deploy? Automated or manual? Who runs it?
- [ ] Config/env vars per environment — how are they set? (ConfigMap, Secrets, Parameter Store)
- [ ] Deployment order (if multiple services — what order matters?)
- [ ] Deployment duration (how long does a full deploy take?)
- [ ] Health check endpoint and how the platform verifies readiness
- [ ] Graceful shutdown handling (in-flight request drainage)
- [ ] Zero-downtime deploy mechanics (rolling update, readiness probe, load balancer drain)
- [ ] Blue/green or canary deployment (if used — how to manage traffic split)

### 6.4 Environment Promotion Flow
- [ ] Exact promotion path: `dev → staging/UAT → pre-prod → production`
- [ ] Gates between environments (QA sign-off, automated test pass, PO approval, security scan)
- [ ] Who can approve promotion to production
- [ ] How promotion is executed (same pipeline? separate trigger? manual approval step?)
- [ ] Hotfix bypass of normal promotion flow — documented procedure

### 6.5 Rollback Procedure
- [ ] How to roll back the **frontend** (previous S3 version, CDN cache, revert container image tag)
- [ ] How to roll back the **backend** (previous Docker image, `kubectl rollout undo`, previous JAR)
- [ ] How to roll back a **database migration** (reversible? Flyway undo? manual rollback SQL? not possible?)
- [ ] Decision criteria: when to roll back vs. hotfix forward
- [ ] Who makes the rollback decision in production
- [ ] Maximum acceptable downtime before rollback is mandatory
- [ ] Rollback testing — has it ever been tested?
- [ ] Data migration rollback — what happens to data written during the bad deploy?

### 6.6 Hotfix Process
- [ ] Hotfix branching strategy (branch from `main`/`master`/tag, not `develop`)
- [ ] Fast-track QA and approval process for hotfixes
- [ ] How to cherry-pick hotfix back to development branch
- [ ] Notification list during hotfix (stakeholders, on-call, support team, customers)
- [ ] Post-hotfix retrospective requirement

### 6.7 Post-Deployment Validation
- [ ] Health check endpoint returns `200 OK`
- [ ] Smoke test suite (automated or manual checklist)
- [ ] Key user journeys verified working
- [ ] No error spikes in logs / monitoring dashboards
- [ ] Database migration applied correctly (verify schema version in migration table)
- [ ] External integrations responding (integration health endpoints)
- [ ] Performance metrics within baseline (response time, CPU, memory, queue depth)
- [ ] Alert channels monitored for 30 min after deploy
- [ ] Deployment announced to team (Slack, email)

### 6.8 On-Call & Incident Response
- [ ] On-call rotation schedule and current on-call person
- [ ] How production alerts are delivered (PagerDuty, OpsGenie, Slack, phone, SMS)
- [ ] Severity classification (P1/P2/P3/P4 or SEV1/SEV2/SEV3/SEV4)
- [ ] Response SLA per severity level
- [ ] War-room / bridge process for P1 incidents (who joins, what channel/call)
- [ ] Incident commander role and responsibilities
- [ ] Communication template for stakeholders during incidents
- [ ] Post-mortem / RCA process (required after P1? Template? Timeline?)
- [ ] Incident log / history (where past incidents are documented)
