## 💡 Tips for a Successful KT

1. **Record every session** (with permission) — you WILL miss things live
2. **Take notes in your own words** — re-explain concepts back to the outgoing dev to verify
3. **Ask "WHY", not just "what"** — understanding intent helps future decisions
4. **Do a practice task each week** — apply learning while help is available
5. **Build YOUR OWN runbooks** — don't rely on theirs, you need to own them
6. **Focus on the 20% that covers 80% of daily work** — prioritize ruthlessly
7. **Shadow a real deployment** before doing one solo
8. **Shadow a real incident** before handling one solo
9. **Get the outgoing dev to review YOUR documentation** — catches gaps
10. **Schedule a "final exam" session** in the last week — go through Phase 10 together

